%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Financial Crisis
  crisisName: Financial Crisis
  resolutionSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 602cff69dded9134ab47a9e6e4be1990, type: 3}
  crisisStartSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 41637ffbd0c9aeb4281489fa8e20f23f, type: 3}
  obviousWarningSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 04fb72efa40378740ad92021cd323cb8, type: 3}
  ominousWarningSplash: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 945c0cc892cb9f74cac246414410623e, type: 3}
  ominousWarningText: "Trade is beginning to falter. Merchants who once extended credit freely now demand coin in advance, while lenders quietly shorten repayment terms and refuse risks they would have accepted only months ago. Warehouses fill with goods that cannot find buyers, and ships remain in harbor longer while captains wait for contracts that never arrive. Wealthy families move their savings into safer holdings, draining coin from markets already struggling to complete ordinary transactions. Officials insist that commerce remains fundamentally sound, but conversations in counting houses grow increasingly nervous. No single institution has failed, yet confidence itself is becoming scarce. The markets have begun to murmur with the sound of fear."
  obviousWarningText: "Credit has collapsed. Merchants rush to recover their coin before more lenders close their doors, while businesses that depended on borrowed money suddenly find themselves unable to pay workers or purchase supplies. Contracts are abandoned, ships sit idle, and markets that once connected distant regions grind toward paralysis. A handful of failures have become a chain reaction as each institution tries to protect itself from the weakness of the next. Crowds gather outside banks and counting houses demanding access to deposits that may no longer exist in liquid form. Trade is no longer merely slowing; confidence in the entire financial system is breaking. What began as uncertainty has become a panic."
  crisisStartText: "Confidence has collapsed, and the financial panic is spreading through the economy. Trade contracts are failing, commercial activity is slowing, and buildings that once generated reliable wealth now struggle to produce the same income. Gold from trade and commerce will remain reduced while the crisis continues, making an economy built heavily around markets especially vulnerable. A strong treasury may soften the blow, while diversified trade and disciplined spending can prevent temporary losses from becoming insolvency. Armies still demand wages, buildings still require maintenance, and the state must continue functioning even as its revenues fall. The crisis will end eventually; the question is what remains when it does."
  resolutionText: "The panic has broken. Whether through a strong treasury, careful reform, or simple endurance, confidence is slowly returning to markets that spent months on the edge of collapse. Merchants resume extending credit, ships return to the routes they abandoned, and counting houses reopen their doors to depositors who once feared their savings were gone. The weakest institutions did not survive, and their failure will be remembered as a lesson written in ledgers for years to come. Wages are paid, contracts are honored, and trade begins, cautiously, to rebuild what panic destroyed. The crisis has ended. What it revealed about the fragility of trust will not be forgotten."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 8
  useAgeWindow: 1
  minimumAge: 10
  maximumAge: 19
  mechanic: 6
